  "note": "Hand truth for Tika's .msg files: the values Apache Tika's own OutlookParserTest asserts of them, at the commit and path below, each written as a JSON pointer into the CLI's message line and the value the CLI's field has when it holds what Tika's assertion holds. Tika's metadata names map to the CLI's fields: TITLE and SUBJECT to /subject, MESSAGE_TO_NAME to a To recipient's name, MESSAGE_TO_EMAIL to its address, FROM_REPRESENTING_NAME and _EMAIL to the sender's (the sender and the represented sender are one person in these files), INTERNET_MESSAGE_ID, IN_REPLY_TO_ID, INTERNET_REFERENCES and CONVERSATION_INDEX to the threading fields, an embedded resource path to an attachment's filename or its embedded message, and ATTACH_FLAGS 4 (ATT_MHTML_REF) to the inline flag. Assertions on content, on the Tika-only metadata, or by prefix only, are not written here. tests/msg.rs reads this file.",
